1
00:00:01,300 --> 00:00:05,320
你们的妈妈去世后 我突然想到了这些童年旧物
So, all this childhood memorabilia came to me after your mother died...

2
00:00:06,300 --> 00:00:08,580
包括日记 相册 可爱的画
diaries, photo albums, adorable drawings.

3
00:00:09,060 --> 00:00:10,920
好好享受你们的回忆之旅吧
So, enjoy your stroll down memory lane,

4
00:00:10,920 --> 00:00:12,460
但请记住 那趟旅程的终点
but know that at the end of that lane

5
00:00:12,460 --> 00:00:14,800
-是垃圾桶 -好吧
- is a dumpster. - Okay.

6
00:00:14,840 --> 00:00:15,868
你在楼上放着一幅画
You have a painting upstairs

7
00:00:15,868 --> 00:00:17,560
是绰号为"冰箱"的威廉·佩利的作品
by William "The Refrigerator" Perry,

8
00:00:17,560 --> 00:00:19,260
但你却没地方存放我的乳牙
but there's no room for my baby teeth?

9
00:00:19,740 --> 00:00:21,940
我需要在车库里腾出一些空间来
I needed to free up some space in the garage.

10
00:00:22,140 --> 00:00:23,760
因为那已经不是车库了
Because it's not a garage anymore.

11
00:00:23,760 --> 00:00:27,100
而是成了堆放没人买的狗床的仓库
It's a warehouse full of dog beds that nobody wants to buy.

12
00:00:27,100 --> 00:00:28,480
最近销售是有些惨淡
It's been a slow period,

13
00:00:28,500 --> 00:00:30,280
但下个季度应该会回升的
but it should pick up next quarter.

14
00:00:30,540 --> 00:00:31,020
怎么回升
What?

15
00:00:31,440 --> 00:00:33,740
等那些狗拿到薪资退税
When all the dogs get back their income tax refunds

16
00:00:34,180 --> 00:00:37,200
就会非常豪爽地去给自己买床吗
and they want to go splurge on beds for themselves?

17
00:00:37,460 --> 00:00:38,220
-乔 -什么事
- Joe. - What?

18
00:00:38,480 --> 00:00:40,759
帮我拖一些这东西到我的车上去
Help me drag some of these things out to my car.

19
00:00:40,759 --> 00:00:43,400
我们今天去做一些老式的营销
We're gonna do some old-fashioned marketing today.

20
00:00:43,400 --> 00:00:45,400
天啊 我们以前的雅达利游戏机
Oh, my God. The old Atari.

21
00:00:45,960 --> 00:00:47,320
还记得我们为什么会有这东西吗
Remember why we got that?

22
00:00:47,380 --> 00:00:50,201
-当然 那是我们第一次享受家庭度假 -第一次
- Yeah. So, we were on our first family vacation ever, okay -- - Ever.

23
00:00:50,201 --> 00:00:51,560
去一个水上公园度假一周
A week at this waterpark resort

24
00:00:51,560 --> 00:00:54,260
-大概才三天爸就觉得无聊了吧 -三天
- and Dad got bored after, what, three days? - Three.

25
00:00:54,320 --> 00:00:55,320
他强迫我们早早离开
Made us leave early,

26
00:00:55,320 --> 00:00:57,000
给我们买了这个来收买我们
and he bought us off with this.

27
00:00:57,000 --> 00:00:58,520
通篇谎言 纯属捏造
Lies and untruths!

28
00:00:58,740 --> 00:00:59,660
我们在那里待了一整周
We stayed the full week,

29
00:00:59,760 --> 00:01:01,919
我还是给你们两个不知感恩的家伙买了那个游戏机
and I got you two ingrates that game anyway.

30
00:01:01,919 --> 00:01:04,340
你还要死不改口多久啊
How long are you gonna stick to that story?

31
00:01:04,340 --> 00:01:06,140
只要你们两个继续把我描绘成
Much as you two enjoy portraying me

32
00:01:06,140 --> 00:01:07,800
虐待孩子的家长 我就继续这么说
as some kind of abusive parent --

33
00:01:09,640 --> 00:01:11,259
放松 乔 我们一会儿就救你出来
Relax, Joe. We'll get you out in a second.

34
00:01:11,259 --> 00:01:14,420
都过去35年了 你还是不肯承认这事
Okay, 35 years, and you -- ugh, you still can't admit it.

35
00:01:14,420 --> 00:01:16,199
-没什么好承认的 -我看到一道光
- There's nothing to admit. - I see light!

36
00:01:16,199 --> 00:01:17,380
我该向它走过去吗
Should I go towards it?

37
00:01:17,380 --> 00:01:20,440
如果不是事实 为何我们姐弟的记忆是一样的 爸
Why would we both remember it one way if it didn't happen, Dad?

38
00:01:20,540 --> 00:01:21,860
小孩子就喜欢编造事情
Kids like to make things up.

39
00:01:22,100 --> 00:01:23,260
他们喜欢那种狗血剧情
They like the drama.

40
00:01:23,740 --> 00:01:24,320
快出来 小子
Come here, kid.

41
00:01:24,631 --> 00:01:28,500
我都快咬断我自己的手臂逃出来了
I was literally about to gnaw my own arm off to get free.

42
00:01:28,500 --> 00:01:29,180
就凭你这小牙齿吗
With those things?

43
00:01:29,180 --> 00:01:31,180
我还保存着你吃棉花糖吃掉的那颗牙齿呢
I still have the tooth you lost in a marshmallow.

44
00:01:31,340 --> 00:01:32,500
你倒是保存了他的牙齿啊
Okay, so, that one you kept?

45
00:01:47,180 --> 00:01:49,000
我去了佛罗里达探望我的父亲
I was in Florida visiting my Dad.

46
00:01:49,280 --> 00:01:50,760
我接到个电话 说他一直在
I'd gotten a call that he was wandering

47
00:01:50,760 --> 00:01:52,800
他过去经营的那个杂货店附近游荡
around the grocery store he used to run.

48
00:01:53,340 --> 00:01:54,938
我想搞清楚他是否没事
I wanted to find out if he was okay,

49
00:01:54,938 --> 00:01:58,204
但是 这种事没办法直接询问
but...that's not something you can just ask.

50
00:01:59,420 --> 00:02:01,580
你妈生前和我每个周日都会来这里
You know, your mother and I came here every Sunday

51
00:02:01,580 --> 00:02:02,900
持续了44年
for 44 years.

52
00:02:03,280 --> 00:02:04,240
你一定很想她吧
You miss her, don't you?

53
00:02:04,480 --> 00:02:05,560
有时会想吧
It comes and goes.

54
00:02:06,620 --> 00:02:08,420
-国庆节那天是最难熬的 -是吗
- Fourth of July is rough. - Really?

55
00:02:08,500 --> 00:02:10,220
我以前都不知道她那么爱国呢
I didn't realize she was so patriotic.

56
00:02:10,340 --> 00:02:13,156
是因为电视上播的那个热狗大胃王比赛
Well, it's that hot dog eating contest they have on TV.

57
00:02:13,156 --> 00:02:15,160
我一直觉得你妈
You know, I always thought that your mother

58
00:02:15,160 --> 00:02:17,020
可以去当大胃王选手
could have been a competitive eater.

59
00:02:17,500 --> 00:02:19,720
我们家从来没有任何食物会过期
No food ever expired in our house.

60
00:02:19,720 --> 00:02:21,721
她只要看到培根
She'd see that last day pop up

61
00:02:21,721 --> 00:02:24,100
或牛奶还有一天就要过期了
on a pound of bacon or a gallon of milk,

62
00:02:24,100 --> 00:02:25,140
就会全部吃下去
and down it went.

63
00:02:25,360 --> 00:02:26,840
她不解决掉心里就不舒服
It was personal for her.

64
00:02:27,700 --> 00:02:28,638
说到食物
Speaking of food,

65
00:02:28,638 --> 00:02:30,880
你后来有没有再去过你那个旧杂货店
y-you ever head over to your old grocery store?

66
00:02:30,880 --> 00:02:32,900
听我说 你还记得那个吗
Hey, listen. Do you remember that?

67
00:02:33,576 --> 00:02:35,760
当然了 企鹅大脚怪
Oh, yeah. Penguinsquatch.

68
00:02:35,760 --> 00:02:37,060
让这座小镇一时名声大噪
Put this town on the map.

69
00:02:38,140 --> 00:02:39,180
1977年6月
June 1977.

70
00:02:39,580 --> 00:02:41,800
一帮开狂欢派对的少年声称有巨大的鸟类脚印
Teen revelers report massive bird footprints

71
00:02:41,800 --> 00:02:43,340
在奥基乔比湖湖岸上出现
emerging from Lake Okeechobee.

72
00:02:43,540 --> 00:02:44,160
人们聚集围观
A crowd gathers,

73
00:02:44,600 --> 00:02:47,140
但是涨潮把所谓的鸟类脚印都冲平了
but the new tide has covered the so-called bird prints,

74
00:02:47,160 --> 00:02:48,700
那些青少年非常受挫
and the teens are beaten soundly.

75
00:02:48,700 --> 00:02:50,520
几天后 又重新出现了这些脚印
Tracks reappear several days later,

76
00:02:50,520 --> 00:02:53,200
再一次地 这消息传遍全镇
and once again, word spreads through town.

77
00:02:53,460 --> 00:02:55,000
一位鸟类学家认为这些脚印
An ornithologist deems the prints

78
00:02:55,000 --> 00:02:57,940
是巨型企鹅的 身高越有15英尺那种
those of a gigantic penguin, some 15 feet in height.

79
00:02:58,260 --> 00:03:00,000
数英里外的人都闻风而来
People come from miles around

80
00:03:00,000 --> 00:03:01,700
就为了看一眼那些神奇的企鹅
to catch a glimpse of the wondrous waddler.

81
00:03:02,140 --> 00:03:04,020
那些脚印出现又消失 持续了好几年
The tracks will appear on and off for years

82
00:03:04,020 --> 00:03:05,620
然后就彻底消失了
and then disappear forever,

83
00:03:06,200 --> 00:03:08,760
但奥会员体操金牌得主玛莉·卢·雷顿
but not before Olympic gold medalist Mary Lou Retton

84
00:03:08,760 --> 00:03:10,839
还是及时地远道赶来 将她的小脚印
makes the trek to place her tiny footprints

85
00:03:10,839 --> 00:03:14,128
踩在了巨型企鹅的脚印里
inside those of the be-flippered colossus.

86
00:03:14,180 --> 00:03:16,200
我们有好几个晚上在那里野餐过吧
Didn't we take a picnic over there a few nights?

87
00:03:16,380 --> 00:03:17,160
大家都去了
Everyone did.

88
00:03:17,160 --> 00:03:21,000
那是我第一次看到你妈吃了一整袋苹果
It's the first time I ever saw your mother eat a bag of apples.

89
00:03:22,294 --> 00:03:26,540
那个 爸 我想问你...
So, Dad, I, uh, I w-- I wanted to ask you --

90
00:03:26,540 --> 00:03:28,520
天啊 不要谈严肃的话题好吗
Oh, boy. No serious talk, okay?

91
00:03:28,740 --> 00:03:31,060
是的 我服了一堆药
Yes, I'm taking all my million pills.

92
00:03:31,440 --> 00:03:33,119
你可以过来按按我的肚子就知道了
You can come over and press my stomach.

93
00:03:33,119 --> 00:03:35,861
我开始觉得自己跟豆袋椅一样了
I'm starting to feel like a bean bag chair.

94
00:03:37,700 --> 00:03:39,398
各位 我刚看到一个鬼魂
Guys, I just saw a ghost.

95
00:03:39,398 --> 00:03:41,558
好了 姑娘们 拿上东西 赶快逃命
Okay, girls, grab your things. We're gone.

96
00:03:41,580 --> 00:03:42,857
不是真正的鬼魂
N-Not a real ghost.

97
00:03:42,900 --> 00:03:44,660
确切地说 是过去的执念
More like a vision from my past.

98
00:03:44,860 --> 00:03:45,700
布兰达·费德曼
Brenda Feldman.

99
00:03:46,240 --> 00:03:49,160
那是曼尼曾经暗恋的一个小姐姐
An older girl that Manny had a crush on.

100
00:03:49,160 --> 00:03:52,500
他小的时候 甚至还给她写过一首诗
He even wrote a poem for her when he was little.

101
00:03:53,340 --> 00:03:54,780
我把我的心给了她
I gave her my heart,

102
00:03:55,100 --> 00:03:57,620
她却送了我一张将我画成老式治安官的画
she gave me a picture of me as an old-time sheriff.

103
00:03:59,680 --> 00:04:01,120
今天是我的第二次机会
Today was my second chance,

104
00:04:01,120 --> 00:04:03,159
但我都没勇气去跟她打招呼
but I couldn't even get up the nerve to say "Hi."

105
00:04:03,159 --> 00:04:05,815
11岁的曼尼一定会觉得我恶心至极
11-year-old Manny would be disgusted by me.

106
00:04:05,815 --> 00:04:08,344
现在你明白12岁的莉莉当时的感受了
Well, now you know how 12-year-old Lily feels.

107
00:04:09,300 --> 00:04:10,520
抱歉 是工作电话
Sorry, this is work.

108
00:04:10,520 --> 00:04:11,520
喂
Hello?

109
00:04:12,020 --> 00:04:14,020
曼尼 你知道这个大家庭里
Manny, you know who this family's

110
00:04:14,020 --> 00:04:16,380
在人际交往问题方面的常驻专家是谁吗
resident expert is in interpersonal problems?

111
00:04:16,480 --> 00:04:17,880
我觉得没人可以...
I would say no one's especially --

112
00:04:17,940 --> 00:04:19,160
没错 正是在下
That's right. It's me.

113
00:04:19,900 --> 00:04:22,300
虽然花了点时间 但我最终说服曼尼相信
It took a little while, but I finally convinced Manny

114
00:04:22,300 --> 00:04:24,820
他上次跟布兰达·费德曼没成的原因
the reason he had failed last time with Brenda Feldman

115
00:04:24,820 --> 00:04:26,560
就在于他用的大招
was because of his grand gesture.

116
00:04:27,440 --> 00:04:29,500
今天需要采用完全不同的方法
Today called for a completely different approach --

117
00:04:30,440 --> 00:04:31,480
超级大招
a super grand gesture.

118
00:04:32,188 --> 00:04:33,580
直接去找她 明白吗
Just go to her, okay?

119
00:04:33,580 --> 00:04:35,360
赶紧上场 冲啊 快
Get in there! Let's go! Come on!

120
00:04:35,360 --> 00:04:36,381
驾
Hyah!

121
00:04:37,240 --> 00:04:41,820
看来我的第一次房屋售卖要泡汤了
Well, looks like my first house sale is going to fall through.

122
00:04:41,980 --> 00:04:43,640
亲爱的 我很遗憾 你知道吗
Oh, sweetie, I'm sorry. You know what?

123
00:04:43,700 --> 00:04:44,740
一定会时来运转的
But things will turn around.

124
00:04:44,860 --> 00:04:45,740
别转回来
Do not turn around.

125
00:04:46,964 --> 00:04:48,520
那是黛布拉·诺克斯
That's Debra Knox.

126
00:04:48,520 --> 00:04:50,820
她抢走了我的"年度最佳教育者奖"
She stole my Educator of the Year Award.

127
00:04:51,060 --> 00:04:52,220
-"阴贼"吗 -影贼
- A swooper?! - A swooper!

128
00:04:52,320 --> 00:04:54,020
-莉莉 拿上东西快逃 -不 不 不是
- Lily, grab your things. - Oh, no, no, no, no.

129
00:04:54,020 --> 00:04:56,960
不是那种会吓坏农场小孩的"影贼"
Not a smoke demon that terrorizes farm children.

130
00:04:57,240 --> 00:05:01,140
是指抢你东西的那种阴险贼子
It's a person that takes things that are supposed to be yours.

131
00:05:01,244 --> 00:05:03,079
我就有个这样的对手
I have one of my own.

132
00:05:03,660 --> 00:05:06,720
我那天就快完成第一次带人看房的工作了
I was closing a deal on my very first showing,

133
00:05:06,720 --> 00:05:09,660
然后一个对手代理人俯冲而下
and a rival agent swooped in.

134
00:05:09,860 --> 00:05:10,820
这房子真漂亮
What a lovely home.

135
00:05:10,920 --> 00:05:12,540
不过或许有些不太适合孩子住
I mean, maybe not great for kids, you know?

136
00:05:12,680 --> 00:05:14,060
等等 什么 我们就快生孩子了啊
Wait, what? But we're pregnant.

137
00:05:14,500 --> 00:05:17,600
天啊 抱歉 我都没看到你们也在这里 我...
Oh, my goodness. I'm sorry. I didn't even see you there. I was --

138
00:05:17,600 --> 00:05:17,900
天啊
Oh, my.

139
00:05:18,240 --> 00:05:20,070
那是加州恶毒黄蜂吗
Is that a California vulture wasp?

140
00:05:20,070 --> 00:05:22,474
肯定是有山狮刚刚在这里捕杀过猎物
A mountain lion must've made a fresh kill.

141
00:05:23,960 --> 00:05:26,920
于是那对夫妻同意晚些时候去她代理的房子里参观
So, the couple agreed to go to her open house later.

142
00:05:27,160 --> 00:05:29,061
♪ 嘿你好 苏 我听说你被甩了 ♪
♪ Hey, there, Sue, I heard you got dumped ♪

143
00:05:29,061 --> 00:05:30,787
♪ 现在你很忧郁 ♪
♪ And now you are blue ♪

144
00:05:30,787 --> 00:05:32,640
♪ 那么我们一起参加毕业舞会怎么样 ♪
♪ So, how 'bout we go to the prom ♪

145
00:05:32,640 --> 00:05:34,560
♪ 前提是我妈她同意 ♪
♪ If it's okay with my mom? ♪

146
00:05:34,620 --> 00:05:38,720
我好庆幸曼尼现在不搞丢人的这套了
I am so glad that Manny stopped doing those embarrassing things.

147
00:05:38,720 --> 00:05:41,140
拜托 谁不喜欢看人放泡妞大招啊
Oh, come on. Who doesn't love a grand gesture?

148
00:05:42,540 --> 00:05:44,620
当着我朋友的面干这种事 罗纳德
In front of my friends, Ronald?!

149
00:05:44,980 --> 00:05:47,220
我真不敢相信我以前会让你帮我做作业
I can't believe I ever let you do my homework!

150
00:05:47,624 --> 00:05:49,240
天啊 不 不 不要
My g-- Oh, gosh. Oh, no, no, Manny!

151
00:05:49,240 --> 00:05:50,680
曼尼 取消 取消行动
Manny, abort, abort, abort.

152
00:05:50,880 --> 00:05:51,140
取消行动
Abort!

153
00:05:51,740 --> 00:05:53,620
退后 退后 退后
Back up! Back up! Back, back, back, back!

154
00:05:53,760 --> 00:05:55,135
-快跑 快跑 -我在跑了
- Keep going! Keep going! - I'm going!

155
00:05:55,135 --> 00:05:55,378
取消行动
Abort!

156
00:05:55,560 --> 00:05:58,920
上周我留了一些狗床在这里
Last week, I left some dog beds here,

157
00:05:58,920 --> 00:06:01,320
现在店家估计收到各种订购请求 忙不过来了
so now the owners are probably getting swamped with requests.

158
00:06:01,560 --> 00:06:02,540
那天我发现
The other day, I found out

159
00:06:02,540 --> 00:06:05,020
乔把六个月的零花钱都存了下来
that Joe saved up six months of allowance

160
00:06:05,020 --> 00:06:06,840
全部捐给了慈善组织
and donated it all to charity.

161
00:06:07,280 --> 00:06:09,560
作为父亲 这属于那种很罕见的时刻
It's one of those rare moments as a dad

162
00:06:09,560 --> 00:06:11,340
就是你会觉得你很失败 没把孩子教好
when you realize you've really dropped the ball.

163
00:06:12,260 --> 00:06:14,940
那孩子需要学会做生意的基本原则
I mean, the kid needed to learn the basics of business.

164
00:06:15,532 --> 00:06:17,660
能把那只狗狗买给我吗
Ooh, can I get that dog?

165
00:06:17,660 --> 00:06:19,373
我可以做50个小时的家务
I'll do 50 hours of chores.

166
00:06:19,373 --> 00:06:20,900
不 100小时也行
No, a hundred.

167
00:06:20,900 --> 00:06:22,280
销售第一课
Sales lesson number one --

168
00:06:22,520 --> 00:06:24,500
在谈判时永远不要显得太急迫
never look desperate in a negotiation.

169
00:06:24,760 --> 00:06:26,600
别带感情 想想你侄女莉莉
No emotion. Think of your cousin Lily.

170
00:06:26,938 --> 00:06:29,500
我看到狗床卖了一些
Hey, I noticed the dog beds moved.

171
00:06:29,500 --> 00:06:31,080
一定很受欢迎吧
They must be pretty popular, huh?

172
00:06:31,280 --> 00:06:33,300
狗狗都不喜欢这些狗床
Um, the dogs didn't like them.

173
00:06:33,500 --> 00:06:35,040
什么 那些都是没人要的狗啊
What? These are dogs nobody wants.

174
00:06:35,120 --> 00:06:36,440
它们是什么情况 这么难伺候
I mean, what do they have going on?

175
00:06:36,520 --> 00:06:38,400
别担心 猫很喜欢这些狗床
Don't worry. The cats love them.

176
00:06:38,720 --> 00:06:40,080
猫 休想 我要把这些狗床拿回家
Cats? Never. I'm taking them home.

177
00:06:40,200 --> 00:06:42,238
猫住在菠萝里 那根本说不通啊
I mean, cat in a pineapple? How does that even make sense?

178
00:06:42,238 --> 00:06:44,885
或许是因为 它们来自"喵威夷"
Maybe...they're from Meow-I?

179
00:06:45,360 --> 00:06:46,920
听懂了吗 夏威夷的梗
Get it? 'Cause Hawaii?

180
00:06:47,172 --> 00:06:49,050
-上车去 -好的
- Get in the car. - Okay.

181
00:06:52,340 --> 00:06:54,640
这个雅达利游戏机有个大凹陷处
This Atari has quite a dent in it.

182
00:06:54,690 --> 00:06:57,021
-你当年用它砸过我吧 -没有的事
- Didn't -- Didn't you throw it at me? - No.

183
00:06:57,312 --> 00:06:59,221
那你解释下我头上的这个凹痕 因为...
Then -- Then explain this groove in my head, 'cause...

184
00:06:59,221 --> 00:07:01,240
你看 严丝合缝 能完美地拼合在一起
Yeah, I can -- I can fit them together like a puzzle.

185
00:07:01,240 --> 00:07:03,840
米奇 你这伤是梦游时摔下楼梯造成的
Mitchell, you fell down the stairs sleepwalking.

186
00:07:03,940 --> 00:07:05,080
那是我们家族遗传性的老毛病了
It's established family history.

187
00:07:05,277 --> 00:07:07,480
不肯承认错误
Unwilling to admit a mistake.

188
00:07:07,480 --> 00:07:09,299
真"好奇"你是从哪学来的呢
Wonder where you picked that up from.

189
00:07:09,299 --> 00:07:12,083
听着 爸从不肯认错 也快把我逼疯了
Look, it drives me nuts, too, that Dad never cops to his mistakes,

190
00:07:12,083 --> 00:07:14,020
但每次都是我们和他各执一词
but it's always gonna be our word against his.

191
00:07:14,020 --> 00:07:16,239
-是啊 -你怎么把这些汗衫的领口都剪开了
- Yeah. - Why did you cut the necks out of all these sweatshirts?

192
00:07:16,239 --> 00:07:18,060
我当年超迷《闪电舞》那部电影
Oh, I was a big "Flashdance" Fan.

193
00:07:18,476 --> 00:07:20,380
你是怎么从霸凌的黄金年代活过来的
How you survived the golden age of bullying,

194
00:07:20,380 --> 00:07:21,940
我永远无法理解
I will never understand.

195
00:07:22,160 --> 00:07:22,980
等等 等等
Wait a minute. Wait a minute.

196
00:07:22,980 --> 00:07:24,880
我们面前就有一堆证据
We are sitting on a treasure trove of evidence

197
00:07:24,880 --> 00:07:28,289
能够证明爸爸强行缩短了我们的假期 好吗
than could prove Dad cut our vacation short, okay?

198
00:07:28,340 --> 00:07:30,160
你知道我的本职工作就是
I mean, you realize that building cases

199
00:07:30,160 --> 00:07:32,420
利用证据来对付社会上最恶劣的罪犯
against society's worst criminals is what I do.

200
00:07:32,420 --> 00:07:34,031
针对那个在湖人队比赛现场外
How's that case against the deaf old lady

201
00:07:34,031 --> 00:07:36,880
售卖培根卷热狗的老太太的案子怎么样了
who sells bacon-wrapped hot dogs outside Laker games going?

202
00:07:36,880 --> 00:07:38,460
已经事先警告过她三次了
She was warned three times.

203
00:07:38,880 --> 00:07:41,940
好吧 我们要怎么证明爸爸强迫我们提早回来
Okay, how do we prove that Dad made us come home early?

204
00:07:41,940 --> 00:07:44,680
我们去的那地方叫什么名字我都忘了
I mean, uh, what was that place we went even called?

205
00:07:44,680 --> 00:07:47,620
等等 我刚看到一个火柴盒
Hold on. I just saw a matchbook from there, and --

206
00:07:47,620 --> 00:07:48,919
找到了 在这呢 就是这个
Okay, yeah, yeah, yeah. Here it is, here it is.

207
00:07:48,919 --> 00:07:51,672
"汉德曼水上公园 25周年纪念"
"Handelman Waterpark. Celebrating 25 years."

208
00:07:52,060 --> 00:07:54,360
我也可以来当回犯罪现场调查员
I can get on this CSI train.

209
00:07:54,360 --> 00:08:00,160
那地方建造于1958年 所以我们是1983年去的
Okay, "Founded in 1958," So that puts us there in '83.

210
00:08:00,520 --> 00:08:02,540
查找我83年的日记
Locating my diary from '83.

211
00:08:02,720 --> 00:08:04,800
-好极了 -很好 找到了
- Okay. - And okay. Here it is.

212
00:08:04,920 --> 00:08:07,500
4月20日 "我觉得JT喜欢我
April 20th. "I think JT likes me.

213
00:08:07,500 --> 00:08:08,849
他嘲笑我头上的凹陷"
Makes fun of my head dent."

214
00:08:08,849 --> 00:08:11,240
好吧 所以度假肯定是在这之前
Alright, so it had to have been before that,

215
00:08:11,240 --> 00:08:12,762
因为当时我们还没有那个游戏机
because we didn't have the video game yet,

216
00:08:12,762 --> 00:08:14,433
所以那个凹...凹...
and that's what made the d-- the -- the --

217
00:08:14,520 --> 00:08:15,460
我打断了你要说的话
I interrupted.

218
00:08:16,360 --> 00:08:18,340
所以我们是4月初去的
So, we were there early April,

219
00:08:18,340 --> 00:08:20,500
没有那个时候的日记记录
and, uh, no diary entries from then.

220
00:08:20,500 --> 00:08:24,040
好吧 但这个或许有帮助
Okay. Okay. But maybe this might help.

221
00:08:24,360 --> 00:08:25,000
瞧瞧这...
Look at...

222
00:08:25,134 --> 00:08:26,438
这里 找到了
Here -- Here it is.

223
00:08:26,438 --> 00:08:28,680
"在汉德曼的第一天"
"Day One at Handelman."

224
00:08:28,680 --> 00:08:29,800
好 来吧
Okay, Here we go.

225
00:08:32,289 --> 00:08:34,429
墨西哥流浪乐队都找来了
A mariachi band?

226
00:08:34,451 --> 00:08:36,100
如果你想追到那个布兰达
If you want the Brenda girl,

227
00:08:36,100 --> 00:08:37,600
装作不在意地和她说话
talk to her like you don't care,

228
00:08:37,900 --> 00:08:40,330
-然后一周都别给她打电话 -怎么
- and then don't call her for a week. - Oh, oh, what?

229
00:08:40,330 --> 00:08:41,925
让他把自己塑造成阴郁神秘的人
And present himself as some brooding mystery man

230
00:08:41,925 --> 00:08:44,602
让她得努力博得他如父亲一般的认可吗
whose dad-like approval she has to work for?

231
00:08:44,720 --> 00:08:46,980
哪个女人觉得那样有吸引力过啊
What woman has ever found that attractive?

232
00:08:47,380 --> 00:08:48,620
我试试看
I'll try it.

233
00:08:49,702 --> 00:08:51,400
太好了 又是黛布拉
Oh, great. There's Debra again.

234
00:08:51,400 --> 00:08:52,640
她八成在下面臭显摆
Probably down there flaunting

235
00:08:52,640 --> 00:08:54,720
她用我的奖赢得的30美元代金券
her $30 gift card she got with my award.

236
00:08:54,780 --> 00:08:56,340
-那是我的奖 -要出击了吗
- It's my award. - Is it go time?

237
00:08:56,760 --> 00:08:57,860
你知道吗 我这就下去
Yeah, you know what? Maybe I will.

238
00:08:57,900 --> 00:08:58,919
我大步流星走到她面前
I'll just march right up to her,

239
00:08:58,919 --> 00:09:01,093
用塔克的招牌盯人术鄙视她
and give her the classic Tucker stare down.

240
00:09:01,500 --> 00:09:03,598
鄙视她 这就是你的大计划
A dirty look. That's your big plan?

241
00:09:03,598 --> 00:09:05,000
是的 她会从我眼中看出
Yeah, she'll see in my eyes

242
00:09:05,000 --> 00:09:06,240
我知道她都做了些什么
that I know exactly what she did,

243
00:09:06,340 --> 00:09:08,680
相信我 不管这商场里
and trust me, all the free sample

244
00:09:08,680 --> 00:09:10,380
有多少免费香水试用
of perfume spritzes in this mall

245
00:09:10,380 --> 00:09:12,720
都遮不住她身上内疚的酸臭味
won't be able to cover up the stench of guilt on her.

246
00:09:12,780 --> 00:09:15,520
我刚刚的闲谈很愉快
Well, I just made a nice little connection.

247
00:09:15,520 --> 00:09:17,340
不是和布兰达聊的 她几乎没注意我
Not with Brenda, who barely noticed me,

248
00:09:17,340 --> 00:09:19,240
是和罗纳德聊的 他邀请我去熊猫快餐
but with Ronald, who invited me to Panda Express

249
00:09:19,240 --> 00:09:20,380
一起化心碎为食欲
so we could eat our feelings.

250
00:09:21,020 --> 00:09:21,440
曼尼
Manny?

251
00:09:22,400 --> 00:09:24,640
我电话号码还没给你 你就走了
Um, you took off before I could give you my number.

252
00:09:25,480 --> 00:09:27,660
也把你的号码给我好吗
And maybe I could get yours, too?

253
00:09:28,080 --> 00:09:29,580
-当然 -好
- Sure. - Yeah?

254
00:09:30,180 --> 00:09:32,960
现在你的问题想要我的建议了吗
Do you need my advice with your problem now?

255
00:09:33,080 --> 00:09:33,560
随便吧
Whatever.

256
00:09:35,990 --> 00:09:37,388
你该一路往西开
See, you should point this thing west

257
00:09:37,388 --> 00:09:39,819
来看看你的曾外孙们
and, uh, come meet your great-grandbabies.

258
00:09:39,819 --> 00:09:41,780
开春了再去吧
Uh, this spring, I think.

259
00:09:41,780 --> 00:09:45,041
我想让宝宝们重现有名的历史老照片
I want to pose them to re-create famous photos from history.

260
00:09:45,041 --> 00:09:48,726
重现《胜利之吻》的服装我准备好了
I've got all the outfits, uh, to re-create the VJ-Day kiss,

261
00:09:48,860 --> 00:09:50,600
但我还需要一顶软呢帽
but I still need the fedora

262
00:09:50,600 --> 00:09:52,780
重现杰克·鲁比击毙李·哈维·奥斯瓦尔德
to pull off Jack Ruby and Lee Harvey Oswald.

263
00:09:53,000 --> 00:09:54,899
-小心 -放心 枪里当然不会有子弹
- Careful. - Well, obviously, the gun won't be loaded.

264
00:09:54,899 --> 00:09:56,375
不 不是 路面有坑
No, no, no. There's a pothole.

265
00:09:56,375 --> 00:09:57,872
老天
Oh, geez.

266
00:09:58,100 --> 00:09:59,220
车胎肯定瘪了
I bet we blew a tire.

267
00:09:59,900 --> 00:10:01,940
幸运的是 某位本地发明家
Fortunately, one local inventor

268
00:10:01,940 --> 00:10:04,760
一直在努力研发专利产品快速千斤顶
has been hard at work on the Presto-Jack TM,

269
00:10:04,760 --> 00:10:07,360
该气动装置既能顶起车身
a pneumatic device that both lifts a car

270
00:10:07,360 --> 00:10:09,420
又能为钻头提供更换车轮螺母的动力
and powers a drill to change lug nuts.

271
00:10:09,500 --> 00:10:11,220
-该不会... -没错
- I don't suppose -- - Yep.

272
00:10:11,360 --> 00:10:12,960
-就在后备箱 -太好了
- In the trunk. - Yes!

273
00:10:12,960 --> 00:10:14,920
我们终于有机会试用了
We can finally test it out!

274
00:10:15,021 --> 00:10:16,300
准备好发射了吗
You ready to launch?

275
00:10:16,300 --> 00:10:17,200
开始吧
Let's do it.

276
00:10:19,580 --> 00:10:23,620
特别稳 抬起来了
Steady as she goes, and she's up!

277
00:10:23,940 --> 00:10:25,680
起效了 你成功了
It's working! You did it!

278
00:10:26,050 --> 00:10:28,460
它 为什么还在上升
It's... Why is it still going?

279
00:10:28,460 --> 00:10:29,620
你按开始键时很用力吗
How hard did you press start?

280
00:10:29,720 --> 00:10:30,640
和那有什么关系
Well, that shouldn't matter!

281
00:10:30,800 --> 00:10:32,940
-按"结束工作"就好 -好的
- Well, just press "End task." - Okay.

282
00:10:33,140 --> 00:10:34,620
但只能按按钮的右半边
But only on the right side of the button.

283
00:10:34,720 --> 00:10:36,336
你为什么不先告诉我
Why wouldn't you tell me that first?!

284
00:10:36,336 --> 00:10:38,554
老天爷啊
Sweet maker!

285
00:10:42,560 --> 00:10:44,320
所有人都警告过我会发生这种事
Everybody warned me this would happen.

286
00:10:49,240 --> 00:10:50,040
黛布拉
Hello, Debra.

287
00:10:51,740 --> 00:10:52,400
小卡
Hi, Cam.

288
00:10:52,480 --> 00:10:53,100
想得美
You wish.

289
00:10:53,340 --> 00:10:55,460
我知道你不会承认 但这双眼睛
I know you'll deny it, but these eyes...

290
00:10:55,460 --> 00:10:57,120
能直接看穿你
can see right through you.

291
00:10:57,300 --> 00:11:00,220
你是指我偷走了年度最佳教育者奖
You mean how I stole the Educator of the Year Award?

292
00:11:00,680 --> 00:11:01,960
我让你承认了
I got you to admit it.

293
00:11:01,960 --> 00:11:03,319
幸好我戴着录音设备
It's a good thing I'm wearing a wire.

294
00:11:03,319 --> 00:11:05,496
-让我看看 -该死的
- Let me see it. - Damn it.

295
00:11:05,900 --> 00:11:08,420
我会穿着这条裙子成为舞会之花
I'm gonna be the belle of the ball in this dress.

296
00:11:08,880 --> 00:11:10,580
偷走这个奖让我有了自信
Stealing this award has given me the confidence

297
00:11:10,580 --> 00:11:12,820
人挡杀人佛挡杀佛
to crush everyone in my path.

298
00:11:15,420 --> 00:11:15,860
不好意思
Permiso.

299
00:11:18,980 --> 00:11:21,000
我根本没见到歌洛莉亚进试衣间
I never even saw Gloria go into the dressing room,

300
00:11:21,000 --> 00:11:22,640
可她就那样出现了 如超级英雄一般
but there she was, like a superhero,

301
00:11:22,800 --> 00:11:25,520
一个亮相就能摧毁别人的自信
able to destroy confidence in a single pose.

302
00:11:26,920 --> 00:11:28,840
我很高兴没买刚才那条裙子
I'm glad I didn't go with the first dress.

303
00:11:29,040 --> 00:11:31,800
他们看一眼这条裙子 就会选我做校长
They'll take one look at this one and make me principal.

304
00:11:33,240 --> 00:11:35,240
-搞什么 -你知道吗
- Aw, come on! - You know what?

305
00:11:35,240 --> 00:11:37,300
或许你该试试那位女士穿的裙子
Maybe you should try the dress on that lady's wearing.

306
00:11:39,720 --> 00:11:42,219
我的天 太天才了 我自叹不如
Oh, my God. That was brilliant and humbling.

307
00:11:42,219 --> 00:11:45,203
我一直以帮别人解决问题而自豪
You know, I-I pride myself on solving people problems.

308
00:11:45,203 --> 00:11:46,420
要知道 你的阴鬼也还没解决
You know what? You still have the swooper.

309
00:11:46,420 --> 00:11:47,660
-或许我可以 -不必了 谢谢
- Maybe I could -- - No, thanks.

310
00:11:49,180 --> 00:11:51,520
她只是不愿意让别人帮她 但我愿意
She just can't accept help, but I can.

311
00:11:51,900 --> 00:11:53,740
我想穿这件大衣跟布兰达约会
I'm thinking about rocking this for my date with Brenda.

312
00:11:54,060 --> 00:11:54,720
先别管这些纽扣
Ignore the buttons.

313
00:11:54,860 --> 00:11:55,920
你能看出这是女式大衣吗
Can you tell this is a woman's coat?

314
00:11:56,480 --> 00:11:56,960
能
Yes.

315
00:11:57,880 --> 00:12:00,240
销售课第二堂课 创造需求
Sales lesson number two -- create demand.

316
00:12:00,840 --> 00:12:03,360
到处放几张狗床 当狗狗爱上它们
Leave a few dog beds lying around, dogs fall in love,

317
00:12:03,580 --> 00:12:05,500
你的电话就会响个不停了
your phones start ringing off the hook.

318
00:12:06,240 --> 00:12:07,540
快去 快
Go ahead. Go.

319
00:12:09,220 --> 00:12:10,660
我的狗狗特别喜欢这张床
My dog really likes this bed.

320
00:12:10,960 --> 00:12:13,380
不知道放在这能不能创造需求
I wonder if leaving it here will create demand.

321
00:12:13,780 --> 00:12:14,860
不用了 谢谢
Uh, no, thank you.

322
00:12:15,977 --> 00:12:17,062
很好的开始
Alright, good start.

323
00:12:17,062 --> 00:12:18,700
你本可以表现得更可爱些
You could've been a little cuter with that.

324
00:12:18,700 --> 00:12:20,678
-什么 -你现在怎么说"特别喜欢"了
- What?! - When did you start saying "Really likes"?

325
00:12:20,678 --> 00:12:22,080
怎么不说"尊稀饭"了
What happened to "Weawwy wikes"?

326
00:12:22,080 --> 00:12:26,060
你请了语言治疗师来羞辱到我不说
You paid a speech therapist to shame it out of me.

327
00:12:26,960 --> 00:12:27,980
还是没有信号
Still no cell service.

328
00:12:28,080 --> 00:12:29,997
我们搭便车去理发店吧
Let's, uh, let's just hitchhike to the barber

329
00:12:29,997 --> 00:12:31,908
在那打电话给拖车公司
and call a tow company from there.

330
00:12:31,920 --> 00:12:33,980
你总是翻旧账
You can't let anything go!

331
00:12:34,020 --> 00:12:36,420
你在我怀孕时跟我妹妹睡了
You slept with my sister while I was pregnant.

332
00:12:36,520 --> 00:12:37,620
又不是性感的那个妹妹
Not the hot one!

333
00:12:37,760 --> 00:12:39,120
我向天发誓 我向天发誓
I swear to God -- I swear to God,

334
00:12:39,120 --> 00:12:40,821
我们一定要办完婚礼 这样等我杀了你
we are going through with this wedding so that I can kill you,

335
00:12:40,821 --> 00:12:42,420
就能跟你的尸体办离婚了
and then I'm gonna divorce your corpse!

336
00:12:42,420 --> 00:12:43,940
一看就知道是恩爱小两口
Well, you seem like a nice couple.

337
00:12:44,500 --> 00:12:45,820
能让我们俩搭个便车吗
Room for two more in there?

338
00:12:45,820 --> 00:12:47,800
我爸的乐观态度
My dad's positive attitude

339
00:12:47,800 --> 00:12:50,220
对抗早晚闹出人命上新闻的情侣
versus a couple bound for a "Dateline" episode?

340
00:12:51,820 --> 00:12:53,220
根本不是一个量级的
It wasn't even a fair fight.

341
00:12:53,531 --> 00:12:56,895
♪ 甜蜜的卡洛琳 ♪
♪ Sweet Caroline ♪

342
00:12:56,895 --> 00:12:59,078
♪ 叭 叭 叭 ♪
♪ Bup-bup-buh ♪

343
00:13:00,704 --> 00:13:05,282
最后一课 总是做好转头走人的机会
Alright. Final lesson -- always be willing to walk away.

344
00:13:06,340 --> 00:13:06,800
罗恩
Hey, Ron.

345
00:13:06,926 --> 00:13:08,814
冲着咱们是老朋友我才先来找你
I'm coming to you first 'cause we're old friends.

346
00:13:08,814 --> 00:13:10,638
-我叫朗恩 -行 听着
- It's Lon. - Yeah. Hey, listen.

347
00:13:10,638 --> 00:13:12,080
这价格是有点贵
It's a steep price on this one,

348
00:13:12,080 --> 00:13:13,020
但这不怪我
but don't blame me.

349
00:13:13,020 --> 00:13:15,840
我的利润其实比做这个的童工还少呢
I'm pocketing less than the kids that, you know, made this thing.

350
00:13:15,980 --> 00:13:17,640
比格犬号已着陆
The Beagle Has Landed.

351
00:13:17,820 --> 00:13:19,258
抱歉 杰 这些都卖不出去
Sorry, Jay, none of these are selling.

352
00:13:19,258 --> 00:13:20,916
长得像烤饼的那些也不行吗
Even the ones that look like hot cakes?

353
00:13:22,980 --> 00:13:24,818
也许养只小狗能让你开心一点
Maybe a puppy will cheer you up.

354
00:13:24,818 --> 00:13:26,570
我告诉过你了 不可能的
I told you, not gonna happen.

355
00:13:26,680 --> 00:13:27,720
你要放弃了吗
You're giving up?

356
00:13:27,720 --> 00:13:29,440
我根本送不出去这些东西
I can't give these things away.

357
00:13:29,860 --> 00:13:31,120
忘了今天我教你的一切吧
Forget everything I taught you today.

358
00:13:31,320 --> 00:13:33,000
我说的那些根本狗屁不通
I don't know what I'm talking about.

359
00:13:34,320 --> 00:13:36,920
先生 我爸爸要给你
Hey, mister, my dad was about to give you

360
00:13:36,920 --> 00:13:38,140
一次千载难逢的好交易
the deal of a lifetime --

361
00:13:38,255 --> 00:13:41,020
一百块就可买到一百张狗床
100 dog beds for a hundred bucks,

362
00:13:41,020 --> 00:13:43,357
这样你每卖一只狗就可送出一张狗床
so you can give one away with each new dog.

363
00:13:43,357 --> 00:13:45,062
一百块 是吗
A hundred bucks, huh?

364
00:13:45,220 --> 00:13:46,860
我看出来你没什么兴趣
I can see you're not serious.

365
00:13:47,980 --> 00:13:49,060
别摇尾巴啦 伙计
Slow down that tail, buddy.

366
00:13:49,240 --> 00:13:50,600
我要把它带走了
This is leaving with me.

367
00:13:52,000 --> 00:13:53,820
慢着 别走啊
Wait, wait. Don't walk away.

368
00:13:54,360 --> 00:13:55,540
五十块怎么样
Would you do 50 bucks?

369
00:13:55,880 --> 00:13:57,020
那你能送我们一只小狗吗
Will you throw in a puppy?

370
00:13:59,202 --> 00:14:01,720
我的晚年做了两个项目
I've had two late-in-life projects.

371
00:14:01,720 --> 00:14:03,740
一个 狗床 是个失败
One, dog beds, was a bust.

372
00:14:03,840 --> 00:14:04,500
另一个
The other...

373
00:14:04,500 --> 00:14:07,480
看起来颇有前景
...is looking pretty promising.

374
00:14:08,417 --> 00:14:09,342
好了
Alright, okay.

375
00:14:09,342 --> 00:14:11,249
那么 汉德曼在99年倒闭了
So, Handelman closed in '99,

376
00:14:11,249 --> 00:14:13,880
所以没有客人登记表能查何时退房的
so no guest registry to tell us when we checked out.

377
00:14:13,880 --> 00:14:15,660
租车公司也是死胡同一条
Rental car companies are a dead end,

378
00:14:15,660 --> 00:14:17,200
也没有信用卡收据
and no credit card receipts.

379
00:14:17,560 --> 00:14:19,720
米奇尔 我们不得不认清现实了
God, Mitchell, it might be time for us to face some facts.

380
00:14:19,820 --> 00:14:21,540
什么现实 上面有人
What? That some people very high up

381
00:14:21,540 --> 00:14:23,080
不想让我们找到真相吗
don't want us to know the truth?

382
00:14:23,760 --> 00:14:26,460
不 是我们得在这件事上放过爸爸了
No. That we might have to let Dad skate on this one.

383
00:14:26,580 --> 00:14:26,920
想都别想
Never.

384
00:14:27,889 --> 00:14:29,932
少吃点泡泡糖香烟 米奇尔
Go easy on those bubble-gum cigarettes, Mitchell.

385
00:14:29,932 --> 00:14:30,960
对身体不好
They're gonna kill you.

386
00:14:30,960 --> 00:14:32,920
听着 我们尝试过了 好吗
Look, we tried, right?

387
00:14:34,600 --> 00:14:36,860
我买过这个泡泡糖香烟
I bought a pack of these

388
00:14:37,200 --> 00:14:38,820
就在咱们待在酒店的最后一晚
the last night we were at that resort

389
00:14:38,820 --> 00:14:42,840
当时我为了在我们去的演唱会上耍帅买的
so I could try to look cool at some... concert that we went to.

390
00:14:42,860 --> 00:14:45,161
等等 它在哪儿呢 我
Hang on. Where was it? I --

391
00:14:45,161 --> 00:14:47,774
中奖 你看到什么了
Oh-ho. Bingo. What do you see, huh?

392
00:14:47,774 --> 00:14:50,280
我在公园 戴着帽子
Uh...um, me at the park in a hat

393
00:14:50,280 --> 00:14:52,239
上面绣着"马多克斯"的名字
with the name "Maddox" embroidered on it.

394
00:14:52,239 --> 00:14:54,640
我都把我的"马多克斯时期"给忘了
Oh, oh, I forgot about my Maddox Pritchett phase.

395
00:14:54,640 --> 00:14:56,120
你不用每天被警察护送去学校
God, it is a miracle that you didn't need

396
00:14:56,120 --> 00:14:57,940
真是个奇迹
a police escort to school every day.

397
00:14:57,980 --> 00:14:59,458
不是看你 是看那个牌子
Not you, the marquee.

398
00:14:59,458 --> 00:15:02,540
-"只有今晚和周三 猴子乐队" -没错
- Uh, "Tonight and Wednesday Only -- The Monkees." - Yes!

399
00:15:02,540 --> 00:15:04,240
根据他们的网站来看
And according to their website,

400
00:15:04,240 --> 00:15:06,080
他们是在14号和16号表演的
they played the 14th and the 16th.

401
00:15:06,080 --> 00:15:07,560
所以 如果我们是第一晚去的
So, if we went the first night,

402
00:15:07,560 --> 00:15:10,580
那就是说我们会在15号离开
that means we would have left the 15th,

403
00:15:10,580 --> 00:15:13,040
也就是提前离开了
and we would have left early.

404
00:15:13,160 --> 00:15:14,038
等一下
Okay, wait just a second.

405
00:15:14,038 --> 00:15:15,386
我记得我很沮丧
I-I remember I was so upset...

406
00:15:15,386 --> 00:15:16,960
-对 -我们的假期被砍掉了
- Yes. - ...that our vacation was being cut short

407
00:15:16,960 --> 00:15:18,400
所以我为了让自己开心一点
that I cheered myself up

408
00:15:18,400 --> 00:15:20,200
去看了《闪电舞》的首映
by going to the premiere of "Flashdance,"

409
00:15:20,200 --> 00:15:21,580
那是在...
which was on...

410
00:15:21,589 --> 00:15:23,131
有了 四月十五日
Ha! April 15th.

411
00:15:23,131 --> 00:15:25,180
太好了 你对这电影是有多爱啊
Yea-- What is up with you and that movie?

412
00:15:25,180 --> 00:15:26,740
她不仅仅是个焊工
She was so much more than a welder,

413
00:15:26,740 --> 00:15:28,560
我也不仅仅是
and I was so much more than the president

414
00:15:28,560 --> 00:15:30,300
反学生周间看电视组织的主席
of Students Against TV on Weeknights.

415
00:15:30,480 --> 00:15:32,060
我知道你是这样记得的
Okay, I know you remember it this way,

416
00:15:32,060 --> 00:15:33,740
但我们怎么证明呢
but how are we gonna prove it?

417
00:15:33,740 --> 00:15:34,140
嘣
Bam!

418
00:15:35,060 --> 00:15:37,104
我的票 清楚地写着"首演之夜"
My ticket, clearly marked "Opening Night."

419
00:15:37,104 --> 00:15:38,900
我要再喊一声"嘣"了
I'm gonna say "Bam" Again.

420
00:15:38,900 --> 00:15:39,420
-嘣 -天哪
- Bam! - Oh!

421
00:15:39,420 --> 00:15:40,440
我简直不敢相信
I can't believe it.

422
00:15:40,440 --> 00:15:42,101
我们终于可以看到爸爸
We might actually see Dad

423
00:15:42,101 --> 00:15:44,320
承认是他的错了
admit that he was wrong! Ah!

424
00:15:44,320 --> 00:15:45,180
我的天 我的天
Oh, my God, oh, my God!

425
00:15:45,280 --> 00:15:47,380
你觉得他会哭吗 别
Do you think he'll cry? No.

426
00:15:47,860 --> 00:15:49,660
克莱尔 别这样 默默享受成功就好
Claire, don't do that. Just take the victory.

427
00:15:49,920 --> 00:15:51,880
为什么 为什么他要这么急着
I mean, why -- why was he in such a rush

428
00:15:51,880 --> 00:15:53,019
回家啊 对吧
to get home, you know?

429
00:15:53,019 --> 00:15:56,160
就为了去欧布莱恩酒吧见他的朋友吗
To -- To meet his buds at O'Brien's Pub?

430
00:15:56,160 --> 00:15:57,740
我不知道 只是...
I don't know. It's just...

431
00:15:57,780 --> 00:15:59,120
这个看起来有点奇怪
Well, that is a little weird, though.

432
00:15:59,120 --> 00:16:00,520
上面写着 "致杰·普里契特
It says, "To Jay Pritchett,

433
00:16:00,820 --> 00:16:02,440
世界上最伟大的酒保
the greatest bartender in the universe.

434
00:16:02,440 --> 00:16:04,700
迪恩·马丁 1983年5月1日"
Dean Martin. May 1, 1983."

435
00:16:04,700 --> 00:16:06,507
爸爸什么时候成酒保了
Since when was Dad a bartender?

436
00:16:06,859 --> 00:16:08,938
等等 这就在我们的旅行之后
Wait, and this is right after our trip.

437
00:16:09,912 --> 00:16:11,227
我给他工作搭档打个电话
I'm calling work wife.

438
00:16:11,840 --> 00:16:12,080
你好
Hello?

439
00:16:12,440 --> 00:16:13,680
你好 玛格丽特 打扰一下...
Hey, Margaret, really quick --

440
00:16:13,920 --> 00:16:15,620
我爸曾经是酒保吗
was Dad ever a bartender?

441
00:16:16,040 --> 00:16:17,160
天哪 谁知道呢
Gosh, who knows?

442
00:16:17,320 --> 00:16:19,520
我反正是不会相信我的记忆了
I wouldn't trust this memory of mine anyway,

443
00:16:19,800 --> 00:16:19,960
而且...
and --

444
00:16:20,673 --> 00:16:22,304
信号好像...
This is a bad connec--

445
00:16:22,304 --> 00:16:23,140
-玛格丽特 -你知道...
- Margaret. - You know --

446
00:16:23,140 --> 00:16:25,360
手机上不再装天线的时候
...that's what a bad connection stopped sounding like

447
00:16:25,360 --> 00:16:26,900
没信号就不是这个声音了
when phones stopped having antennas.

448
00:16:27,640 --> 00:16:28,000
好吧
Fine.

449
00:16:28,660 --> 00:16:29,780
你爸早年开公司的时候
Early days of the business,

450
00:16:29,780 --> 00:16:31,140
我们发不出工资
we couldn't make payroll.

451
00:16:31,320 --> 00:16:32,660
他不得不中断当时的旅行
He had to come back from a trip

452
00:16:32,660 --> 00:16:34,820
自掏腰包来给员工发工资
to pay everyone out of his own pocket.

453
00:16:34,820 --> 00:16:37,640
还要做夜班工作来补上缺口
Took the night job to make ends meet.

454
00:16:37,700 --> 00:16:39,300
他怎么不告诉我们呢
Why wouldn't he have told us?

455
00:16:39,440 --> 00:16:41,040
可能不想让你们担心吧
Probably didn't want to worry anyone.

456
00:16:41,560 --> 00:16:44,660
总之 在穷途末路之际 他有了最佳的杰作
Anyway, back to the wall, he did some of his best work.

457
00:16:44,660 --> 00:16:46,669
设计出卖得最好的衣柜
Came up with a best-selling closet.

458
00:16:46,905 --> 00:16:49,347
《欢迎 马多克斯》
"Introducing the Maddox."

459
00:16:52,320 --> 00:16:55,020
转角处就是家庭聚餐厨房
And around this corner is the entertainer's kitchen.

460
00:16:55,580 --> 00:16:56,377
你在这里干嘛
What are you doing here?

461
00:16:56,377 --> 00:17:00,763
我刚从这个不安全的后门进来的
Oh, I just came through the un-secure back door.

462
00:17:01,120 --> 00:17:02,138
又见面啦
Hello, again.

463
00:17:02,138 --> 00:17:04,520
你好 你的房子我们还是很有兴趣
Hi. We're still interested in your house.

464
00:17:04,520 --> 00:17:06,660
只是我们可能会更倾向这间
We just might be leaning towards this one.

465
00:17:06,660 --> 00:17:08,140
我真是太惊讶了
Oh, I'm very surprised.

466
00:17:08,620 --> 00:17:10,980
像你们这样这么爱做饭的人
People that like cooking so much --

467
00:17:10,980 --> 00:17:14,740
真的会满意这么小的食品储藏区...
are you guys going to be happy with this tiny, little pantry...

468
00:17:15,220 --> 00:17:17,560
后面的这个这么大的储藏间吗
that leads to a gigantic pantry?

469
00:17:17,800 --> 00:17:19,500
准备好要看看互动式育婴房了吗
Are you ready to see the interactive nursery?

470
00:17:19,760 --> 00:17:20,999
宝宝兴奋地踢了一下呢
The baby just kicked!

471
00:17:20,999 --> 00:17:22,700
你们好啊
Oh. Hey.

472
00:17:22,700 --> 00:17:25,140
我们... 你们要成为我的新邻居了吗
We... Are you all about to be my new neighbor?

473
00:17:25,820 --> 00:17:27,820
希望你们也喜欢开派对 我叫弗莱德
Hope you like to party. My name's Fred.

474
00:17:27,920 --> 00:17:30,720
他们都叫我偷窥哥... 不过理由不重要啦
They call me Peeper because -- well, that doesn't matter.

475
00:17:30,720 --> 00:17:32,880
你... 快来看 是巧克力碎饼干
Oh, you -- look, it's chocolate chip cookies!

476
00:17:32,880 --> 00:17:34,040
孩子们 快进来
Kids, get in here!

477
00:17:34,080 --> 00:17:35,480
快来这吃你们的晚饭
Get yourself some supper!

478
00:17:37,100 --> 00:17:38,420
这两位是我的心肝宝贝
These are my blessings.

479
00:17:38,500 --> 00:17:40,660
我是不是喜欢异族女子 我认罪
Do I like ethnic women? Guilty.

480
00:17:40,806 --> 00:17:43,440
你们喜欢新鲜下的蛋吗
Do you like farm-fresh eggs?

481
00:17:43,440 --> 00:17:47,840
我卖掉了我第一间房子并灭掉了我的阴贼
I sold my very first house and destroyed my swooper.

482
00:17:47,980 --> 00:17:50,300
当然啦 唯一能灭掉真正影贼的方法
Of course, the only way you can destroy a real swooper

483
00:17:50,300 --> 00:17:52,499
是在秋分前后的满月日刺死它们的影子
is to stab its reflection during the Harvest Moon.

484
00:17:52,499 --> 00:17:54,649
祝你们在波兰愉快啊 两位
Enjoy Poland, you two!

485
00:17:54,742 --> 00:17:57,380
弗兰克 我可能得关门了
Hey, Frank. Afraid I was about to close up.

486
00:17:57,380 --> 00:17:59,872
-贝琪今天生日 -好吧 那我们下回再来啦 唐
- Betsy's birthday. - Okay, we'll come back, Don.

487
00:17:59,872 --> 00:18:02,022
别 别着急 我的剪刀功夫还不错啊
Well, h-hang on. I'm -- I'm pretty nifty with the shears.

488
00:18:02,022 --> 00:18:03,600
我以前都会帮卢克剪头发
I used to -- I used to cut Luke's hair,

489
00:18:03,600 --> 00:18:05,060
有一次还把家里院子发现的刺猬
and I once trimmed a hedge in our yard

490
00:18:05,060 --> 00:18:07,609
从刺猬头剪成明星的柔顺长发
into the spitting image of Doug Henning.

491
00:18:07,715 --> 00:18:08,600
成功打动我
Sold.

492
00:18:08,600 --> 00:18:10,410
-那你们好了帮忙锁门 -谢谢你啦
- Just lock her up. - Thank you very much.

493
00:18:11,480 --> 00:18:12,700
请上座啊 少年
Hop on up there, young man.

494
00:18:14,400 --> 00:18:16,800
要是我没记错 你人生第一次看到裸女
If I'm not mistaken, you saw your first naked lady

495
00:18:16,800 --> 00:18:18,720
-就是在这间理发厅 -你很内行
- in this barbershop. - You know it.

496
00:18:19,840 --> 00:18:22,100
很棒的交通指挥员 但一旦她开始发疯
Hell of a crossing guard, but when she went crazy,

497
00:18:22,100 --> 00:18:23,220
她就会一条路走到底
she didn't go halfway.

498
00:18:23,440 --> 00:18:24,580
毕竟人家职业就没有在走一半的
Well, that was her training.

499
00:18:25,693 --> 00:18:26,765
老爸
So, Dad, um...

500
00:18:29,947 --> 00:18:31,549
我就直言不讳了
just gonna get this over with.

501
00:18:31,931 --> 00:18:32,960
天啊 你不会是要问我
Oh, boy. Is this gonna be

502
00:18:32,960 --> 00:18:34,678
跑回去超市的那件事吧
about me going back to the grocery store?

503
00:18:34,678 --> 00:18:37,189
毕竟事情真的有点奇怪嘛...
Well, it -- it just seemed a little weird.

504
00:18:37,440 --> 00:18:39,000
我听说你在那里游荡了几个小时
I heard you were there for hours.

505
00:18:39,140 --> 00:18:40,480
那里简直一团乱
The place was a mess.

506
00:18:40,540 --> 00:18:42,520
超市人的荣誉心呢
I mean, where is the pride?

507
00:18:43,000 --> 00:18:45,620
想当年 他们每周二都会外送橙子来给我
Old days, they used to deliver my oranges on Tuesdays.

508
00:18:45,620 --> 00:18:47,621
就算有一万个希伯来奴隶
I could not have built a pyramid faster

509
00:18:47,621 --> 00:18:49,840
我造金字塔也没那么快
with 10,000 Hebrews.

510
00:18:49,840 --> 00:18:51,040
所以你其实不是在游荡吗
So, you weren't just wandering?

511
00:18:51,820 --> 00:18:54,180
我只是... 我很想念以前的那一切
It's just -- I miss it, is all.

512
00:18:54,980 --> 00:18:56,720
那我要问下一题了
This takes me to my next question.

513
00:18:57,440 --> 00:19:00,559
你跟老妈有没有...
Um...did you and Mom ever --

514
00:19:00,559 --> 00:19:03,173
想要过另一个孩子
ever want a-a-another child?

515
00:19:03,173 --> 00:19:04,700
我想天下的父母都有好奇过
Well, I suppose all parents wonder

516
00:19:04,700 --> 00:19:07,041
如果生的是不同的孩子 一切会变怎么样吧
how things would have changed if they had a different child.

517
00:19:07,041 --> 00:19:08,494
我不是说有一个不同的孩子啦
I-I didn't -- didn't mean a different one.

518
00:19:08,494 --> 00:19:10,601
我是说除了我之外 再有一个
I-I mean an additional one.

519
00:19:11,140 --> 00:19:12,140
怎么会这么问
Why do you ask?

520
00:19:12,384 --> 00:19:14,538
因为如果你有另一个孩子
Well, 'cause if you'd had another kid,

521
00:19:14,538 --> 00:19:16,476
或许... 或许他就会接手你的生意
maybe -- maybe he'd have taken over the business

522
00:19:16,476 --> 00:19:18,013
那你就不用把生意卖掉了
and -- and you wouldn't have had to sell.

523
00:19:18,013 --> 00:19:19,013
我一直...
I always --

524
00:19:19,100 --> 00:19:21,160
一直有点内疚我没接下来
I always felt kind of bad that I didn't.

525
00:19:22,580 --> 00:19:24,880
菲尔 答案是没有 从没想过
The answer is no, Phil. Never.

526
00:19:27,220 --> 00:19:27,660
因为...
Because...

527
00:19:27,660 --> 00:19:30,300
其实你有把家庭事业接手过去啊 不是吗
well, you did take over the family business, didn't you?

528
00:19:30,540 --> 00:19:33,600
保持快活人生 为所有人带来欢乐
Keeping life light, making it fun for everybody.

529
00:19:35,760 --> 00:19:37,000
名师出高徒嘛
I learned from the best.

530
00:19:39,140 --> 00:19:41,360
在我成长的期间 他一直是最酷的爸爸
When I was growing up, he was the cool dad.

531
00:19:41,580 --> 00:19:42,300
他很潮
He was hip.

532
00:19:42,760 --> 00:19:44,500
他会歌舞电影《油脂》中所有的舞步
He knew all the dances from "Grease."

533
00:19:44,720 --> 00:19:45,800
他也熟悉各种流行语缩写
He knew all the expressions.

534
00:19:46,360 --> 00:19:47,900
BFF 一辈子的死党
BFF -- best friends forever.

535
00:19:48,340 --> 00:19:49,620
TMI 分享太多隐私了
TMI -- too much information.

536
00:19:49,820 --> 00:19:50,740
BJ 蓝色牛仔裤[口交]
BJ -- blue jeans.

537
00:19:51,100 --> 00:19:52,240
这让我一直觉得自己很幸运
It makes me feel lucky.

538
00:19:53,660 --> 00:19:55,140
那天我们其实没做什么特别的 但...
We didn't do much that day, but...

539
00:19:55,140 --> 00:19:58,100
或许那是我此生与我父亲共度过...
it might have been one of the -- the best days

540
00:19:58,100 --> 00:19:59,100
最美好的日子之一吧
I ever had with my dad.

541
00:20:01,160 --> 00:20:02,820
只是当时并不知道会是最后一天
I just didn't know it would be the last.

542
00:20:04,020 --> 00:20:05,300
我爸走得安详
My dad was okay.

543
00:20:05,900 --> 00:20:09,260
与他共处的那天让我学到的是
And my takeaway from our day --

544
00:20:10,440 --> 00:20:14,080
不要错过对你喜爱的人表达爱的...
Don't miss a chance to let the people you appreciate...

545
00:20:14,080 --> 00:20:15,820
机会
know that.

546
00:20:16,899 --> 00:20:18,500
其实最难的东西呢
The hard part has been, um,

547
00:20:18,500 --> 00:20:21,180
是要想出一个点子来向我爸致意
figuring out a way to pay tribute to my dad,

548
00:20:21,180 --> 00:20:24,300
不过那天在车库里我终于来了灵感
but something came to me in the garage today.

549
00:20:30,320 --> 00:20:31,600
我觉得他会喜欢我的点子
I think he would have liked it.

550
00:20:44,200 --> 00:20:46,500
我的父亲 他留下的巨大足迹
He left some big footprints, my old man.

551
00:20:49,814 --> 00:20:52,220
你看 他们处得很愉快
Look, they are getting along great.

552
00:20:52,220 --> 00:20:53,020
这不是我们需要担心的
It's not our worry.

553
00:20:53,360 --> 00:20:54,300
应该担心的是你妈
Your mother is.

554
00:20:54,940 --> 00:20:57,200
八年了 她忽视斯黛拉 令她有心病
Eight years, she ignored Stella, and gave her a complex.

555
00:20:57,580 --> 00:20:59,440
有一次我在咔咔按我的笔
One time I was clicking a pen,

556
00:20:59,660 --> 00:21:00,500
斯黛拉都吐了
Stella threw up

557
00:21:00,500 --> 00:21:01,940
因为她以为是你妈穿着高跟鞋朝她走来
because she thought high heels were coming.

558
00:21:02,660 --> 00:21:03,060
我回来啦
Hola.

559
00:21:05,180 --> 00:21:06,240
这是什么
What is this?

560
00:21:07,071 --> 00:21:08,700
他才是负责的大人
He is the grown up.

561
00:21:08,700 --> 00:21:10,160
亲爱的 我们知道你对...
Honey, we know how you feel...

562
00:21:10,240 --> 00:21:14,020
这真是我此生最可爱的宝贝了
It's the cutest thing in my whole life.

563
00:21:14,200 --> 00:21:15,819
我爱你
I love you.

564
00:21:15,819 --> 00:21:20,506
天啊 我要跟我最乖的崽自拍 我马上回来
Oh my God, I need a selfie with my best little boy. I will be back.

565
00:21:20,940 --> 00:21:21,900
不是你的错
It's not your fault.

566
00:21:23,520 --> 00:21:25,970
这不是你的错
It's not your fault.
